type: software
title: "QaraamiGen: computational ethnomusicology tools for Somali qaraami music"
authors:
  - family-names: Ibrahim
    given-names: Khalid
    email: hrgysa123@gmail.com
    city: Minneapolis
    country: US
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-09"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/khalid-ibrahim/somali-music-archive"
keywords:
  - Somali music
  - qaraami
  - computational ethnomusicology
  - music generation
  - MusicGen
  - LoRA fine-tuning
  - pentatonic conformity
  - music transcription
abstract: >-
  Open-source research code for preserving and studying Somali qaraami music:
  corpus inventory and clip preparation, LoRA fine-tuning of MusicGen on
  archival recordings under a corrected training harness, a pentatonic
  conformity metric, held-out per-song evaluation, preference optimisation,
  cassette restoration experiments, and a local inference service. The
  source recordings and the trained weights are not distributed.
